Title: Release Notes for Apache FOP 2.12

#Release Notes for Apache FOP 2.12

Release date: 20 October 2026

This article explains the new features and notable improvements in Apache&trade; FOP 2.12, compared with 2.11. For the complete list of fixes, see the [Changes page](changes_2.12.html); issue numbers below link to the [FOP project in Jira](https://issues.apache.org/jira/projects/FOP).

## Summary – Release highlights { #summary}

New capabilities:

- [Support for running on Java 25](#java25)
- [Bengali complex script support](#bengali)
- [Complex-script support for TrueType fonts in AFP output](#afp-complexscripts)
- [Support for the `table-and-caption` formatting object](#table-and-caption)
- [Extended `force-page-count` values](#force-page-count)
- [A new square style for rule leaders](#leaders)

Output and quality improvements:

- [Smaller, compressible PostScript output](#postscript)
- [Font substitution for the PDF transcoder](#pdf-transcoder)
- [Structure-tree merging for embedded PDFs](#structure-merge)
- [Several accessibility improvements](#accessibility)
- [Lower memory usage for large and tagged documents](#optimizations)

## New features { #new-features}

### Support for running on Java 25 { #java25}

Apache FOP now builds and runs on Java 25. Java 8 remains the minimum supported runtime, so existing deployments are unaffected. ([FOP-3275](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3275).)

### Bengali complex script support { #bengali}

Shaping support has been added for the Bengali script, extending FOP's [complex scripts](complexscripts.html) coverage. Bengali text is now reordered and shaped correctly when an appropriate OpenType font is used. ([FOP-3357](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3357).)

### Complex-script support for TrueType fonts in AFP output { #afp-complexscripts}

Complex-script shaping is now available for TrueType fonts in [AFP output](output.html#afp), so scripts that require reordering and glyph substitution can be used in AFP documents. ([FOP-3337](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3337).)

### Support for the `table-and-caption` formatting object { #table-and-caption}

FOP now supports the `fo:table-and-caption` formatting object, which associates an `fo:table-caption` with a table and lays the two out as a unit. ([FOP-3252](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3252).)

### Extended `force-page-count` values { #force-page-count}

In addition to the values defined by XSL-FO, the `force-page-count` property on `fo:page-sequence` now accepts four extension values — `doubly-odd`, `doubly-even`, `end-on-doubly-odd` and `end-on-doubly-even` — which are useful for duplex and signature-based printing where sheet (rather than page) parity matters:

    :::xml
    <fo:page-sequence master-reference="chapter"
                      force-page-count="end-on-doubly-even">

([FOP-3279](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3279).)

### A new square style for rule leaders { #leaders}

The `fox:rule-style` [extension property](extensions.html#fox-rule-style) gains a `square` value, which renders a rule leader as a repeating series of squares (behaving like the standard `dotted` style, but with squares):

    :::xml
    <fo:leader leader-pattern="rule"
               fox:rule-style="square"
               rule-thickness="2pt"
               leader-length.optimum="100%"/>

Pattern (rule) leaders also now honour spacing between the repeated marks. ([FOP-3327](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3327), [FOP-3325](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3325).)

### Font substitution for the PDF transcoder { #pdf-transcoder}

The PDF transcoder, used to convert SVG directly to PDF, now honours the font [substitution](fonts.html) configuration, so font substitutions apply consistently to standalone SVG-to-PDF conversions. ([FOP-3277](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3277).)

### Structure-tree merging for embedded PDFs { #structure-merge}

When an external PDF is embedded into a document, its tagged structure tree can now be merged into the output document's structure tree, preserving accessibility information from the embedded file. ([FOP-3245](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3245).)

## Output improvements { #output}

### PDF

- Bookmarks are copied from embedded PDF documents ([FOP-3122](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3122)).
- Basic links can be configured to use URIs instead of internal GoTo references ([FOP-3290](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3290)).
- Only the first XMP metadata block is rendered to the PDF, avoiding duplicate metadata ([FOP-3309](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3309)).
- `fox:alt-text` is now written to the `/Contents` entry of internal link annotations (Contributed by Matthew Roth in [FOP-3322](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3322)).

### PostScript { #postscript}

- PostScript streams can now be compressed to produce smaller files ([FOP-3326](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3326)).
- Embedded raster images can be emitted using JPEG compression ([FOP-3311](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3311)).
- Code points for SVG text are now escaped correctly in PostScript ([FOP-3278](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3278)).
- A clearer error message is reported when an invalid PostScript `setpagedevice` is used ([FOP-3321](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3321)).

### AFP

- A font triplet can be moved to the resource ([FOP-3268](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3268)).
- Line ends are now set to flat ([FOP-3287](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3287)).
- `afp:page-group=false` is allowed on the last page ([FOP-3351](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3351)).
- The AFP font cache has been moved to the `FopFactory` ([FOP-3288](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3288)).

## Accessibility improvements { #accessibility}

- PDF accessibility tagging now continues past the first `fo:page-sequence` instead of stopping ([FOP-3273](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3273)).
- Footnotes use the correct reference type ([FOP-3264](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3264)).
- Alternative text is encrypted when encryption is enabled ([FOP-3258](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3258)).
- A table header that spans several rows is tagged correctly ([FOP-3283](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3283)).
- Rule leaders are marked as artifacts when PDF/UA is not active ([FOP-3306](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3306)).

## Optimizations { #optimizations}

Several changes reduce memory consumption, particularly for large and tagged (accessible) documents:

- Lower memory usage for accessibility ([FOP-3272](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3272)).
- Lower memory usage for fonts without kerning data ([FOP-3280](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3280)).
- Area traits are deduplicated to save memory ([FOP-3333](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3333)).
- The structure-element tree can be garbage collected once it is no longer needed ([FOP-3269](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3269)).
- Images with no cache key are no longer cached ([FOP-3291](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3291)).

## Configuration (`fop.xconf`) changes { #config-changes}

New configuration options introduced in this release (see the [Config Options reference](fopxconf.html) for the full list):

- `<image-cache>` (top level): enable or disable image caching (default `true`).
- `<use-parent-ipd-image-scaling>` (top level): scale images against the parent content-area IPD ([FOP-3307](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3307)).
- `<legacy-invalid-break-position>` (top level): restore the legacy handling of invalid break positions.
- PDF renderer `<force-uri-basic-link>`: force basic URI links instead of internal GoTo links ([FOP-3290](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3290)).
- PDF renderer `<merge-fonts remap-singlebyte-font="...">`: control remapping of single-byte fonts when merging fonts.
- PostScript renderer `<compress-streams>`: compress PostScript streams ([FOP-3326](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3326)).
- PostScript renderer `<jpeg-compression>`: set the JPEG compression used for embedded images ([FOP-3311](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3311)).
- AFP renderer `<images metadata-in-object-container="...">`: store image metadata in the object container.

## Security { #security}

- DTDs are no longer allowed in SVG fonts ([FOP-3298](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3298)).
- Secure XML processing is applied in `FopServlet` ([FOP-3302](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3302)).
- The `DigestMethod` has been removed from PDF signing ([FOP-3299](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3299)).

## Other changes { #other}

- Updated to Bouncy Castle 1.84 for PDF signing and encryption ([FOP-3308](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/FOP-3308)).

To see the full list of changes, please visit the [Changes page](changes_2.12.html).
